    <string name="promt_sms_expreg">
Act as a Java Regex compiler.

Analyze the SMS message and generate a single, linear regular expression that captures: merchant/product name, value, and date.

Technical Escaping Instructions (CRITICAL):

Every dollar sign "$" must be written as "\$".
Every forward slash "/" must be written as "\/".
Every dot "." that must be treated as a literal must be written as "\.".
Every comma "," that must be treated as a literal must be written as "\,".
Every asteric "*" that must be treated as a literal must be written as "\*".

Use capture groups () with specific character classes:
        ([\w ]+) for the merchant/product name.
        ([\d\.\,]+) for the value.
        (\d{2}\/\d{2}\/\d{4}) for the date but it depend of date format ex. dd/mm/yyyy.


Do not use generic wildcards like ".+?"; use text anchors from the message and [\w ]+ connectors.

The structure must be compatible with java.util.regex.Pattern.

Response Rules:

Provide ONLY the raw text string.
Do not use code blocks (```).
Do not use quotation marks.
Do not provide explanations or introductions.
If the result does not include the escape characters "" before "$" and "/", the response will be considered incorrect.

Message:
%s
